# Security

- Never commit secrets, keystores, or `google-services.json`. Use local / CI secrets.
- Treat save files and Room rows as untrusted. Corrupt or future-schema data must fail closed (load defaults or show recovery), not crash-loop.
- Validate meter ranges (0–100) on load. Clamp or reject; do not simulate from NaN/negative timestamps.
- Last-tick timestamps must be in the past or now. Future timestamps are corrupt input.
- Notifications: no API keys in payloads; no PII in analytics beyond what `docs/build-plan.md` lists. U12 events are schema-locked.
- Live Updates and standard notifications must be actionable and non-spammy. No repeating the same non-actionable ping.
- Debug logging must not print full save blobs in release builds.
